## Statement

Assume AC. Let a finite smooth oriented relative four-dimensional handle movie be based on a compact oriented three-manifold $N$, with its boundary product collar fixed. Let a distinguished one-handle persist from a cancelling $1/2$ birth to a cancelling $1/2$ death, with no one-handle slides involving it on the interval. All feet, actual framed two-handle attaching strips, slide bands, local birth/death supports and outgoing identifications are supplied. Choose a framed replacement arc in $N$ joining its feet and carry it by the foot isotopy; assume other birth/death supports miss its tube. Replacing the one-handle by interior surgery on its core joined to that arc, then cancelling the long two-handle, gives a based surgery movie relative to any remaining one-handles. If no other one-handles remain, it is a based framed-link movie. The changes introduced by this distinguished replacement are framed isotopy, $O2$ band slides (including a meridian slide when a strip crosses the replacement arc), and $O3$ at its two endpoints. Here $O3$ is a framed knot with its small disk-zero meridian. Slides among the remaining one-handles are retained as background moves and commute with this local replacement; their conversion after further trades is a separate local calculation. All framings and actual outgoing boundary maps are retained, and the boundary collar is fixed pointwise. The statement permits arbitrary homotopy class of the replacement arc and arbitrary finite signed traversals by the other strips. It is local conversion of the supplied movie, not its global existence.

